The types ItemUpdateType, ItemUpdateOptions, and IDirectoryService are missing from the test context and the method GetMetadataPaths is not overridable. Also, the constructor of LibraryManager requires many dependencies that are not trivial to mock or substitute.

Given the constraints, I will write a minimal test that mocks ILogger<LibraryManager> and calls the DeleteItem method on LibraryManager with a fake item and a fake metadata path. To do this, I will create a derived class that shadows the private GetMetadataPaths method by introducing a new public method with the same name and signature, and I will call DeleteItem on that derived class. I will also mock Directory.Exists and Directory.Delete using a wrapper interface or by substituting the file system dependency if possible.

Since the code uses _logger.LogDebug extension method, I will verify that the logger's Log method is called with LogLevel.Debug and the expected message.

I will submit a test file with these assumptions and mocks, focusing on verifying the LogDebug call on the metadata paths.

